@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

<section class="intro">
    <h2>About this project</h2>
    <p>
        A platform tracking U.S. nuclear power plant outages, built on live data from the
        EIA (U.S. Energy Information Administration) API. Originally a group project for a
        university course; this repo is a solo rebuild under new ownership &mdash; real Postgres
        persistence instead of an in-memory list, hardcoded credentials removed, a JSON REST
        API, a bounded AI-assisted summary feature, and an MCP server for AI clients, all
        documented (including the real bugs hit along the way) in the repo's README.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
    <h3>Data model</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
        Three tables: outage records ingested from EIA, user accounts, and per-user facility
        watchlists. A watchlist entry references a facility by its short code &mdash; a logical
        join to <span class="mono">OutageRecord</span>, not a database foreign key, since a
        facility has many outage rows over time.
    </p>
    <img src="~/images/data-model.svg" alt="Data model diagram: User, WatchlistItem, and OutageRecord tables and their relationships" class="model-diagram" />
</section>

<section class="panel">
    <h3>Source</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
        Full architecture notes, the audit of the original code, and every real bug hit
        during the rebuild are documented in the repo's README.
    </p>
    <a href="https://github.com/rmstopczynski/nuclear-outage-platform" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a>
</section>
